++USERMOD(ZMG0001)      /* BREXX/370 TSO INTEGRATION */ .
++VER(Z038) FMID(EBB1102) PRE(UY16532)
 /*
   PROBLEM DESCRIPTION:
     TSO ON MVS 3.8J HAS NO REXX.  THIS USERMOD LETS THE EXEC
     COMMAND RUN REXX EXECS THROUGH BREXX/370
     (GITHUB.COM/MVSLOVERS/BREXX370).

     IKJCT430 (EXEC) ASKS THE NEW CSECT IKJCT437 WHETHER AN EXEC IS
       REXX AND LETS IT RUN THE EXEC THROUGH BREXX IF SO:
       IMPLICIT (%NAME OR NAME): SEARCHED IN SYSUEXEC, SYSUPROC,
         SYSEXEC, SYSPROC, AS BREXX SEARCHES FOR RX.  A MEMBER IN
         SYSUEXEC OR SYSEXEC IS REXX; A MEMBER IN SYSUPROC OR
         SYSPROC IS REXX ONLY IF LINE 1 IS A COMMENT CONTAINING
         "REXX".  OTHERWISE A SYSUPROC MEMBER IS PASSED OVER AND A
         SYSPROC MEMBER RUNS AS A CLIST.
       EXPLICIT EXEC 'DS(MEMBER)': REXX IF LINE 1 IS SUCH A
         COMMENT, WHATEVER LIBRARY THE DATA SET IS; OTHERWISE A
         CLIST.
       EXPLICIT EXEC ... EXEC: THE NEW EXEC KEYWORD (ABBREVIATIONS
         E, EX, EXE) RUNS THE MEMBER AS REXX.  AN UNQUALIFIED NAME
         THEN GETS THE SUFFIX .EXEC INSTEAD OF .CLIST.
       NOT FOUND: A COMMAND THAT A RUNNING CLIST ISSUES AND THAT
         DOES NOT EXIST GETS IKJ56479I (... NOT FOUND OR REXX
         IDENTIFIER IS MISSING) INSTEAD OF IKJ56500I, WITH A HINT
         ON THE SECOND LEVEL.  THIS IS WHAT A REXX EXEC WITHOUT
         THE REXX COMMENT, RUN AS A CLIST, TYPICALLY RUNS INTO.
       OPERANDS: THE EXEC GETS ITS ARGUMENT AS ON Z/OS.  IMPLICIT:
         THE OPERANDS AFTER THE NAME WITHOUT LEADING AND TRAILING
         BLANKS, OTHERWISE AS TYPED (QUOTES KEPT).  EXPLICIT: THE
         QUOTED VALUE LIST AS TYPED, OUTER QUOTES OFF AND ''
         HALVED, CASE AND INNER BLANKS KEPT.  NO OPERANDS, OR '',
         IS NO ARGUMENT.  CLISTS RECEIVE THEIR PARAMETERS AS BEFORE.
       THESE ARE THE TSO/E RULES AS MEASURED ON Z/OS, EXCEPT THAT
         THE USER LIBRARIES ARE SEARCHED WITHOUT ALTLIB.
     IKJCT437 FINDS AND READS THE MEMBER ITSELF (BPAM) AND LINKS
     THE BREXX COMMAND PROCESSOR WITH A CPPL OF ITS OWN.

   SPECIAL CONDITIONS:
     ACTION:
       THE USERMOD IS ACTIVE AT ONCE (SYS1.CMDLIB), NO IPL IS
       NEEDED - UNLESS THE APPLY TAKES A NEW EXTENT OF
       SYS1.CMDLIB: A MEMBER IN A NEW EXTENT CANNOT BE LOADED
       THROUGH THE LINK LIST UNTIL THE NEXT IPL (IEA703I 106-F).
       COMPARE THE EXTENTS BEFORE AND AFTER THE APPLY.
     ACTION:
       BACK UP SYS1.CMDLIB(EXEC,EX) BEFORE THE APPLY.  DO NOT
       ACCEPT THIS SYSMOD.  TO REMOVE IT, RESTORE IT AND COPY THE
       BACKUP BACK; RESTORE NEEDS UY16532 ACCEPTED.
     ACTION:
       ZMG0001 (BREXX/370), ZMG0002 (REXX/370) AND ZMG0003 (BOTH)
       CHANGE THE SAME ELEMENTS AND EXCLUDE EACH OTHER.  RESTORE
       THE ONE INSTALLED BEFORE APPLYING ANOTHER.
     DEPENDENCY:
       BREXX/370 MUST BE INSTALLED IN THE LINK LIST (LOAD MODULE
       BREXX) AT A LEVEL THAT TAKES ITS ARGUMENT FROM THE COMMAND
       BUFFER (BREXX370 #358).  WITHOUT BREXX EXEC STAYS
       CLIST-ONLY.
     PREREQUISITES:
       UY16532 (IKJCT430): THE OBJECT DECK SHIPPED HERE IS THAT
       LEVEL PLUS THE HOOKS.  THE REST OF THE LOAD MODULE IS KEPT
       AS INSTALLED.
     RESTRICTION:
       AN EXPLICIT EXEC OF A SEQUENTIAL DATA SET ALWAYS RUNS AS A
       CLIST; REXX EXECS MUST BE PDS MEMBERS.  THE ARGUMENT OF AN
       EXPLICIT EXEC LOSES ITS LEADING AND TRAILING BLANKS.

   COMMENTS:
     BREXX/370 TSO INTEGRATION, MVSLOVERS, BY MIKE GROSSMANN.
     IKJCT430 IS THE ONE OF ZMG0002 (REXX/370) UNCHANGED.

     THE FOLLOWING MODULES ARE AFFECTED BY THIS USERMOD:
     MODULES:
       IKJCT430  IKJCT437 (NEW)
     LOAD MODULES:
       EXEC (SYS1.CMDLIB)
 */ .
++JCLIN .
//ZMGLK01  EXEC PGM=IEWL,PARM='LIST,XREF,LET,RENT,REUS'
//SYSPRINT DD  SYSOUT=*
//AOST4    DD  DISP=SHR,DSN=SYS1.AOST4
//SYSLMOD  DD  DISP=SHR,DSN=SYS1.CMDLIB
//SYSLIN   DD  *
  ORDER IKJCT431,IKJCT430,PARS,IKJCT432,IKJCT435,IKJCT437
  INCLUDE AOST4(IKJCT430,IKJCT431,IKJCT432,IKJCT435,IKJCT437)
  ENTRY IKJCT430
  ALIAS EX
  NAME EXEC(R)
/*
++MOD(IKJCT430) DISTLIB(AOST4) .
<<DECK IKJCT430>>
++MOD(IKJCT437) DISTLIB(AOST4) .
<<DECK IKJCT437>>
